            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, I am afraid so. The `recent_files` built-in section has only the [following arguments](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a0edfb3a16533fb7335295f4554d81408301599d/doc/mini-starter.txt#L366-L371).\r\n\r\nAnother approach would be to ensure that certain files are not saved (or present at the time of `recent_files` is executed) in the `v:oldfiles` variable.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, I am afraid so. The <code class=\"notranslate\">recent_files</code> built-in section has only the <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a0edfb3a16533fb7335295f4554d81408301599d/doc/mini-starter.txt#L366-L371\">following arguments</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Another approach would be to ensure that certain files are not saved (or present at the time of <code class=\"notranslate\">recent_files</code> is executed) in the <code class=\"notranslate\">v:oldfiles</code> variable.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Yes, I am afraid so. The recent_files built-in section has only the following arguments.\nAnother approach would be to ensure that certain files are not saved (or present at the time of recent_files is executed) in the v:oldfiles variable.",
